{"name":"Dollar","hex":"#7d8774","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Dollar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A small town in Clackmannanshire council area, Scotland","An unincorporated community in Coosa County, Alabama, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Dollar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dollar","blocks":[{"text":"Dollar is the name of more than 25 currencies and their base units. The United States dollar, named after the international currency known as the Spanish dollar, was established in 1792 and is the first so named that still survives. Others include the Australian dollar, Brunei dollar, Canadian dollar, Eastern Caribbean dollar, Hong Kong dollar, Jamaican dollar, Liberian dollar, Namibian dollar, New Taiwan dollar, New Zealand dollar, Singapore dollar, Trinidad and Tobago dollar, and several others. The symbol for most of those currencies is the dollar sign $; the same symbol is used by many countries using peso currencies."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ad/Joachimsthaler_1525.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dollar"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Dollar_du_Sarawak.jpg/500px-Dollar_du_Sarawak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Dollar_du_Sarawak.jpg/500px-Dollar_du_Sarawak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One Sarawak dollar from 1935, featuring Charles Vyner Brooke, the 3rd and last White Rajah of Sarawak","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADollar_du_Sarawak.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Philip_V_Coin_silver%2C_8_Reales_Mexico.jpg/500px-Philip_V_Coin_silver%2C_8_Reales_Mexico.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pa